 "level_notes": {
  "0": "A theoretical model: level 0 lists mechanised metatheory (Isabelle AFP Pi_Calculus and Psi_Calculi), verification tools built on the calculus (Mobility Workbench, ProVerif for the applied pi-calculus, TyPiCal) and small interpreters; Pict is the classic programming language built on the asynchronous pi-calculus.",
  "1": "Defined by Milner, Parrow and Walker, \"A Calculus of Mobile Processes I/II\" (1989 LFCS reports, 1992 Information and Computation). Variants (polyadic, asynchronous, applied) have their own defining papers."
 },
